s-than-truckload and other truck transportation, rail intermodal, air cargo, ocean cargo, expedited ground and air delivery of time-critical freight, heavy-haul/specialized, hazardous materials, cold chain/temperature-controlled, U.S.-Canada and U.S.-Mexico cross-border, intra-Mexico, intra-Canada, project cargo, and customs brokerage services, as well as transportation services to other transportation companies, such as third party logistics and less-than-truckload service providers. This segment serves the automotive parts and assemblies, consumer durables, building products, metals, chemicals, foodstuffs, heavy machinery, retail, electronics, military equipment and general commodities industries. The Insurance segment provides risk and claims management services; and reinsures risks of its independent contractors. The company markets its services through a network of agents, third party capacity providers, and employees. Landstar System, Inc. was founded in 1988 and is headquartered in Jacksonville, Florida.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Frank A. Lonegro | President, CEO & Director | Age 56 | Compensation: $1.1M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 1K people. Revenue per employee of $3.6M ranks in the top quartile among Industrials peers. Each employee generates $165K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $5K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 0\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags low compensation governance risk (3/10).","financial_summary":["Landstar System, Inc. is a mid-cap industrials business with a $5.0B market cap on $4.7B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at -14% over the past three years and +4% annually across the full decade, and a shrinking top line is the hardest headwind any business can overcome.","Returns on capital run at 45% against a 9% cost of capital \u2014 a 36-point spread that is the clearest signature of an economic moat.","The business throws off $215M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 5 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 1.96\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, the balance sheet carries net cash, which is the gold standard: the business never has to make desperate decisions in a bad year, and interest coverage of 27\u00d7 is fortress-like.","Management returns a meaningful 6.0% of market cap to owners through dividends and buybacks, a strong signal of disciplined capital allocation, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome, and profit capture is only 0.3\u00d7 the fair share, suggesting no structural edge inside its industry."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Revenue growth in the bottom decile of Industrials peers \u2014 losing share inside the profit pool","sev":"red","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Low reinvestment-driven growth suggests the compounding engine has stalled","sev":"amber","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Carries a 43% premium to sector median EV/EBITDA (confirmed by 1 other valuation measure)","sev":"amber","cat":"valuation","magnitude":0.43308157099697886},{"text":"Piotroski score 4/9 \u2014 below the median for a healthy business","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Above-average short interest at 5.9% of float","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Significant insider selling (net $2.0M)","sev":"amber","cat":"insider","dollars":-2035709.16},{"text":"Industrials sector lagging the market significantly, underperforming by 6% over 3 months","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Cyclicality and capital intensity \u2014 order books turn on a dime, and the heavy fixed cost base that creates the moat also magnifies the downturn.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Tariff and trade-policy exposure \u2014 industrial exporters sit squarely in the crosshairs of protectionist policy, and retaliatory tariffs can close markets without warning.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Altman Z comfortably in the safe zone \u2014 a fortress balance sheet on this measure","20 consecutive years of dividend payments \u2014 an operating record that makes the dividend claim credible","Healthy payout ratio leaves room for both dividend growth and reinvestment","ROIC sits in the top quartile of Industrials peers \u2014 the moat is wider than the neighbourhood","Among the least levered in Industrials \u2014 the fortress balance sheet in its peer set","Minimal goodwill on the balance sheet \u2014 low impairment risk"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Landstar System (NASDAQ:LSTR) Stock Gets Price Target Reduction from Morgan Stanley","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/11/landstar-system-nasdaqlstr-stock-gets-price-target-reduction-from-morgan-stanley.html","date":"2026-11-11","timestamp":1794420409.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.318,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["analyst_action"]},{"title":"Will Earnings And Dividend Affirmation Change Landstar System (LSTR) Narrative","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/transportation/nasdaq-lstr/landstar-system/news/will-earnings-and-dividend-affirmation-change-landstar-syste","date":"2026-11-10","timestamp":1794271252.985,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.813,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings","dividend"]},{"title":"Trading the Move, Not the Narrative: (LSTR) Edition","source":"news.stocktradersdaily.com","link":"https://news.stocktradersdaily.com/news_release/132/Trading_the_Move,_Not_the_Narrative:_LSTR_Edition_110926070802_1794226082.html","date":"2026-11-09","timestamp":1794226082.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.0,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"UPS Stock And O